<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Appendix</h2>

<section id="A1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Proof Sketch for Theorem 1</h3>

<div id="A1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here we provide a sketch of the proof for the Causal Generalization Bound. The full proof builds on the PAC-Bayesian framework for meta-learning.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<ol id="A1.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Setup:</span> We define a prior distribution <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(f)</annotation></semantics></math> over the space of reasoning functions <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>. A key insight is that our prior is informed by the causal graph, <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(f)=P(f|\hat{\mathcal{G}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(f)=P(f|\hat{\mathcal{G}})</annotation></semantics></math>. We assume that functions consistent with the true causal graph <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> have higher prior probability.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">PAC-Bayes Bound:</span> The standard PAC-Bayes theorem states that for any posterior distribution <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Q</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q(f)</annotation></semantics></math> over functions, with probability <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A1.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}_{f\sim Q}[\mathcal{L}_{query}(f)]\leq\mathbb{E}_{f\sim Q}[\hat{\mathcal{L}}_{supp}(f)]+\sqrt{\frac{KL(Q||P)+\log(m/\delta)}{2m-1}}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>Q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mi>K</mi><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mi>log</mi><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}_{f\sim Q}[\mathcal{L}_{query}(f)]\leq\mathbb{E}_{f\sim Q}[\hat{\mathcal{L}}_{supp}(f)]+\sqrt{\frac{KL(Q||P)+\log(m/\delta)}{2m-1}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> is the size of the support set. We choose <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> to be the posterior distribution after observing the support set data.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Connecting KL Divergence to Graph Structure:</span> The crucial step is to bound the <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="KL(Q||P)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">KL(Q||P)</annotation></semantics></math> term. Our prior <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math> is centered around functions consistent with <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The data from the support set, generated according to the true graph <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>, will push the posterior <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="Q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>Q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">Q</annotation></semantics></math> towards functions consistent with <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. The ”distance” between these two distributions, measured by the KL divergence, can be shown to be proportional to the structural disagreement between <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\mathcal{G}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\mathcal{G}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}^{*}</annotation></semantics></math>. We can bound this using information-theoretic arguments:</p>
<table id="A1.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E5.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="KL(Q||P)\leq\alpha\cdot d_{SHD}(\hat{\mathcal{G}},\mathcal{G}^{*})+\beta" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mi>L</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Q</mi><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mo>,</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">KL(Q||P)\leq\alpha\cdot d_{SHD}(\hat{\mathcal{G}},\mathcal{G}^{*})+\beta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\beta</annotation></semantics></math> are constants related to the complexity of the function class. The Structural Hamming Distance (<math id="A1.I1.i3.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{SHD}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{SHD}</annotation></semantics></math>) counts the number of edge additions, deletions, or reversals needed to transform one graph into another.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">4.</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Combining Terms:</span> Substituting this bound back into the main PAC-Bayes inequality and simplifying the terms yields the final result presented in Theorem 1. This formalizes the intuition that a mistake in the causal graph discovery phase (a larger <math id="A1.I1.i4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{SHD}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{SHD}</annotation></semantics></math>) will necessarily lead to a looser generalization bound and potentially worse performance.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Implementation Details</h3>

<div id="A1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The pseudocode for the <span id="A1.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">CSML</span> meta-training loop is provided in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ A.2 Implementation Details ‣ Appendix A Appendix ‣ Causal-Symbolic Meta-Learning (CSML): Inducing Causal World Models for Few-Shot Generalization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> <span id="alg1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">CSML</span> Meta-Training Algorithm</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.6" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
              
            Meta-training task distribution <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p(\mathcal{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p(\mathcal{T})</annotation></semantics></math>, learning rates <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha,\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha,\beta</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
              
            Initialize parameters for <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{enc}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{enc}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{reason}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{reason}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              
            <span id="alg1.l3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">while</span> not converged <span id="alg1.l3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              
              Sample a meta-batch of tasks <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\mathcal{T}_{j}\}_{j=1}^{B}\sim p(\mathcal{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>B</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\mathcal{T}_{j}\}_{j=1}^{B}\sim p(\mathcal{T})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              
              Initialize a global symbol set <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}_{global}\leftarrow\emptyset" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}_{global}\leftarrow\emptyset</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l6.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each task <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l6.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              
               Collect symbols from support set: <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}_{j}\leftarrow\phi_{enc}(\mathcal{D}_{j}^{supp})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}_{j}\leftarrow\phi_{enc}(\mathcal{D}_{j}^{supp})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}_{global}\leftarrow\mathbf{Z}_{global}\cup\mathbf{Z}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∪</mo><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}_{global}\leftarrow\mathbf{Z}_{global}\cup\mathbf{Z}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l9.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l9.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l10.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Outer loop: Update causal graph
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              
              Update causal graph <math id="alg1.l11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}</annotation></semantics></math> by solving Eq. <a href="#S3.E1" title="In Causal Induction Module (ϕ_{𝑐⁢𝑎⁢𝑢⁢𝑠⁢𝑎⁢𝑙}). ‣ 3.1 Architectural Components ‣ 3 The CSML Framework ‣ Causal-Symbolic Meta-Learning (CSML): Inducing Causal World Models for Few-Shot Generalization" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> on <math id="alg1.l11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{Z}_{global}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐙</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{Z}_{global}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
              
              
              Initialize meta-loss <math id="alg1.l12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{meta}\leftarrow 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{meta}\leftarrow 0</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
              
              
              <span id="alg1.l13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each task <math id="alg1.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{T}_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{T}_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l13.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
              
              
               <span id="alg1.l14.3" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg1.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> Inner loop: Adapt reasoning module
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg1.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
              
              
               Clone reasoning parameters: <math id="alg1.l15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta^{\prime}_{reason}\leftarrow\theta_{reason}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta^{\prime}_{reason}\leftarrow\theta_{reason}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16:</span></span>
              
              
               For <math id="alg1.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N_{inner\_steps}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>N</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>_</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N_{inner\_steps}</annotation></semantics></math>:

</div>
<div id="alg1.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
              
              
               <math id="alg1.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}_{j}^{supp}\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{\mathcal{T}_{j}}(\phi_{reason}(\phi_{enc}(\mathcal{D}_{j}^{supp}),\mathcal{G});\theta^{\prime}_{reason})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mi>j</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}_{j}^{supp}\leftarrow\mathcal{L}_{\mathcal{T}_{j}}(\phi_{reason}(\phi_{enc}(\mathcal{D}_{j}^{supp}),\mathcal{G});\theta^{\prime}_{reason})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l18" class="ltx_listingline">
